mpic trials.  After winning the 100 metres three days earlier at Stockholm, Craig was favored."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The six semi-finals advanced the winner of each heat to the final, with Applegarth and Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/70456"} "Richard Rau"] " joining four Americans, including Craig, to compete for the gold medal.  In the final, Applegarth led coming off the turn, but was soon passed by Craig and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78705"} "Donald Lippincott"] ".  The finish was close, but Craig held off a fast-finishing Lippincott to win the sprint double.  Lippincott added the 200 silver medal to the bronze medal he had won in the 100."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/61691"} "Ralph Craig"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "22.8 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "21.9 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "21.7 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78705"} "Donald Lippincott"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "22.8 (1 h11)"] [:td {} "21.8 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "21.8 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/68844"} "Willie Applegarth"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "24.7 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "21.9 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "21.9 (3)"] [:t